This extension adds Balatro modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Installs Lovely-Injector and SteamModded.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00][size=3]This extension will automatically download and install [url=https://github.com/ethangreen-dev/lovely-injector]Lovely-Injector[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/balatro/mods/45]SteamModded[/url] for the user, which are required by almost all mods.[/size][/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*][b][color=#ea9999]❌Game Pass version is NOT currently supported. [/color][/b]This is due to Lovely-Injector and SteamModded not yet supporting the Xbox Game Pass version.[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Lovely-Injector installs to the game folder, recognised by a "winmm.dll" file.[/*]
[*]SteamModded mods with a "tk_debug_window.py" file install to the "%APPDATA%\Balatro\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Malverk (Texture Pack Manager) mods with a "malverk.lua" file install to the "%APPDATA%\Balatro\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Mods are recognised by a ".lua" file and an "assets", "libs", "localization", "lovely", "lsp_def", "api" or "utils" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs Lovely-Injector (to game folder) and SteamModded (to Mods folder).[/*]
[*]You can download the latest Lovely-Injector and Malverk (Texture Pack Manager) using the buttons in the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Balatro mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Lovely-Injector:

Recognised when the archive contains a "winmm.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

SteamModded:

Recognised when the archive contains a "tk_debug_window.py" file.

  Installs to: "%APPDATA%\Balatro\Mods"

========================================================================

Malverk (Texture Pack Manager):

Recognised when the archive contains a "malverk.lua" file.

  Installs to: "%APPDATA%\Balatro\Mods"

========================================================================

Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".lua" file and a "assets", "libs", "localization", "lovely", "lsp_def", "api" or "utils" folder.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
